Great question — Persian (Farsi) is where a lot of popular embedding models fall apart, so you need a genuinely multilingual model. Here are the best options, all of which integrate cleanly with Spring AI:

## 🥇 Recommended options

### 1. If you can use a paid API → **OpenAI `text-embedding-3-large`**
Strong multilingual performance (including Persian), zero infrastructure, and it's the most battle-tested integration in Spring AI.

```yaml
spring:
  ai:
    openai:
      api-key: ${OPENAI_API_KEY}
      embedding:
        options:
          model: text-embedding-3-large
          dimensions: 1024   # optional: shrink from 3072 to save vector DB space
```

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.ai</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-ai-starter-model-openai</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

An alternative in this category is **Google's `gemini-embedding-001`** (supports 100+ languages, 3072 dims, available via Spring AI's Google GenAI module) or **Cohere `embed-multilingual-v3`** via the Bedrock integration — Cohere's multilingual models are explicitly trained on Persian.

### 2. If you want self-hosted / free → **BGE-M3 via Ollama** ⭐ (my pick for your case)
`BAAI/bge-m3` is consistently the best open-source multilingual embedding model — it's trained on 100+ languages including Persian, handles 8,192-token inputs, and in independent benchmarks it beats even `text-embedding-3-large` on non-English retrieval. Since user prompts may contain sensitive data, keeping embeddings local is a nice bonus.

```bash
ollama pull bge-m3
```

```yaml
spring:
  ai:
    ollama:
      base-url: http://localhost:11434
      embedding:
        options:
          model: bge-m3
```

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.ai</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-ai-starter-model-ollama</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

### 3. Persian-specialized option → **`heydariAI/persian-embeddings`**
A fine-tuned XLM-RoBERTa model built specifically for Persian + English semantic search. It's available in GGUF format on Ollama Hub, so it works with the same Spring AI Ollama starter as above. Worth benchmarking against BGE-M3 on *your* data if Persian quality is the top priority.

### 4. Fully embedded (no external service) → **Spring AI Transformers (ONNX)**
Spring AI can run ONNX embedding models in-process via `spring-ai-starter-model-transformers`. You could load a multilingual model like `intfloat/multilingual-e5-base` or IBM's `granite-embedding-107m/97m-multilingual` (both explicitly support Persian). Good for simple deployments, but the runnable model must be exported to ONNX.

## Practical advice

- **Best overall for your case:** BGE-M3 on Ollama if you can self-host; `text-embedding-3-large` if you'd rather not manage anything.
- **Whatever you pick, use ONE model for everything** — vectors from different models aren't comparable, and switching later means re-embedding all stored prompts.
- **Code stays portable:** you only depend on Spring AI's `EmbeddingModel` interface, so swapping providers is a config change:

```java
@Autowired
EmbeddingModel embeddingModel;

float[] vector = embeddingModel.embed("متن کاربر یا English text here");
```

- **Quick sanity test for Persian quality:** embed a Persian sentence and its English translation — a good multilingual model will give them high cosine similarity (cross-lingual alignment), which BGE-M3 and text-embedding-3-large both do well.

